{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "import math\n\ndef is_not_prime(n) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if n is not prime, False if n is prime.\"\"\"\n    # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are not prime by definition.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n    # Check for divisors from 2 up to the integer square root of n.\n    limit = math.isqrt(n)\n    for d in range(2, limit + 1):\n        if n % d == 0:\n            return True\n    # If no divisors are found, the number is prime.\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "def differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(a, b) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True when integers a and b differ in exactly one bit position; otherwise False.\"\"\"\n    xor_result = a ^ b\n    set_bits_count = bin(xor_result).count('1')\n    return set_bits_count == 1"}
