{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth Newman-Conway number using memoization.\n\n    This function calculates P(n) where P(1)=1, P(2)=1, and P(n) = P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)) for n > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Initialize a dictionary for memoization with the base cases.\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def compute(k: int) -> int:\n        # Return the cached value if already computed.\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # Compute the value using the recurrence relation and store it in the cache.\n        val = compute(compute(k - 1)) + compute(k - compute(k - 1))\n        memo[k] = val\n        return val\n\n    # Begin computation for the requested 'n'.\n    return compute(n)"}
