{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the Eulerian number A(n, m) using recursion with memoization.\n    Validates inputs and handles base cases and recurrence relation.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or not isinstance(m, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs n and m must be integers.\")\n\n    if n < 0 or m < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs n and m must be non-negative.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        if m != 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"If n is 0, m must also be 0, but got m={m}.\")\n    else:  # n > 0\n        if not (0 <= m < n):\n            raise ValueError(f\"If n is {n}, m must be between 0 and {n-1} (inclusive), but got m={m}.\")\n\n    _eulerian_cache = {}\n\n    def _compute_eulerian_recursive(current_n, current_m):\n        if (current_n, current_m) in _eulerian_cache:\n            return _eulerian_cache[(current_n, current_m)]\n\n        result = 0\n        if current_n == 0 and current_m == 0:\n            result = 1\n        elif current_n > 0 and (current_m < 0 or current_m >= current_n):\n            result = 0\n        else: # current_n > 0 and 0 <= current_m < current_n\n            term1 = (current_n - current_m) * _compute_eulerian_recursive(current_n - 1, current_m - 1)\n            term2 = (current_m + 1) * _compute_eulerian_recursive(current_n - 1, current_m)\n            result = term1 + term2\n\n        _eulerian_cache[(current_n, current_m)] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _compute_eulerian_recursive(n, m)"}
