{"task_id": "Mbpp/108", "solution": "def _all_integers(lst) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in the given list are integers.\"\"\"\n    return all(isinstance(x, int) for x in lst)\n\ndef _validate_inputs(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"Validates that all inputs are lists and contain only integers.\"\"\"\n    for lst in [list1, list2, list3]:\n        if not isinstance(lst, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"All arguments must be lists.\")\n        if not _all_integers(lst):\n            raise ValueError(\"All list elements must be integers.\")\n\ndef _merge_elements(list1, list2, list3) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Merges elements from three lists into a single new list.\"\"\"\n    return list1 + list2 + list3\n\ndef _sort_elements(elements) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order and returns a new list.\"\"\"\n    return sorted(elements)\n\ndef merge_sorted_list(list1, list2, list3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Merges three lists into a single sorted list, preserving duplicates.\n    Raises TypeError if an argument is not a list, or ValueError if a list contains non-int elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_inputs(list1, list2, list3)\n    merged_list = _merge_elements(list1, list2, list3)\n    sorted_list = _sort_elements(merged_list)\n    return sorted_list"}
