{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the common elements in given nested lists, validating input and handling edge cases.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _validate_input(nested_lists):\n        \"\"\"Ensures nested_lists is a list of lists and raises TypeError for invalid inputs.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(nested_lists, list):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list of lists.\")\n        for inner_list in nested_lists:\n            if not isinstance(inner_list, list):\n                raise TypeError(\"All elements in the outer list must be lists.\")\n\n    def _compute_intersection(nested_lists):\n        \"\"\"Computes the intersection of elements across all inner lists, short-circuiting for empty lists.\"\"\"\n        if not nested_lists:\n            return set()\n\n        # Initialize the intersection with the first list, converting to a set\n        # to handle duplicates within the list and for efficient set operations.\n        common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n        # Short-circuit if the first list is empty, as the intersection will then be empty.\n        if not common_elements:\n            return set()\n\n        # Iterate through the rest of the lists and compute the intersection.\n        for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n            current_list_set = set(nested_lists[i])\n            common_elements.intersection_update(current_list_set)\n            # If at any point the intersection becomes empty, further intersections\n            # will also be empty, so we can short-circuit.\n            if not common_elements:\n                return set()\n\n        return common_elements\n\n    _validate_input(nested_lists)\n    return _compute_intersection(nested_lists)"}
