{"task_id": "Mbpp/279", "solution": "def is_num_decagonal(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth decagonal number using the formula D(n) = 4*n^2 - 3*n.\n    Raises ValueError if n is not a positive integer (n < 1).\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n < 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer (n >= 1).\")\n\n    # Compute the decagonal number using the given formula.\n    return 4 * n**2 - 3 * n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/283", "solution": "def validate(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the frequency of each digit in the integer is less than or equal to the digit itself.\n    This function uses a nested helper to count digit frequencies.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _countDigits(abs_n_val):\n        \"\"\"Counts the frequency of each digit in a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        counts = [0] * 10\n        if abs_n_val == 0:\n            counts[0] = 1\n            return counts\n        while abs_n_val > 0:\n            abs_n_val, digit = divmod(abs_n_val, 10)\n            counts[digit] += 1\n        return counts\n\n    abs_n = abs(n)\n    counts = _countDigits(abs_n)\n\n    for d in range(10):\n        # For each digit d, if it appears in the number (counts[d] > 0)\n        # and its frequency is greater than the digit itself, return False.\n        if counts[d] > 0 and counts[d] > d:\n            return False\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/282", "solution": "def sub_list(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Subtracts two lists element-wise.\n    Raises ValueError for unequal lengths or non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, list) or not isinstance(b, list):\n        raise ValueError(\"Inputs must be lists.\")\n\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input lists must be equal length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        val_a = a[i]\n        val_b = b[i]\n\n        if not isinstance(val_a, (int, float)) or not isinstance(val_b, (int, float)):\n            raise ValueError(\"All elements must be numeric.\")\n\n        result.append(val_a - val_b)\n    return result"}
