{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(arr1, arr2, n) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size n.\n    Assumes lists contain numeric elements and are sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    class LengthMismatchException(Exception):\n        \"\"\"Custom exception for when array lengths do not match expected 'n'.\"\"\"\n        def __init__(self, message: str):\n            super().__init__(message)\n\n    class InputValidator:\n        \"\"\"Utility class for validating input arrays.\"\"\"\n        @staticmethod\n        def validate_length(arr: list, expected_n: int) -> None:\n            \"\"\"Validates if the array's length matches the expected size 'n'.\"\"\"\n            if len(arr) != expected_n:\n                raise LengthMismatchException(f\"Array length mismatch: expected {expected_n}, got {len(arr)}\")\n\n    InputValidator.validate_length(arr1, n)\n    InputValidator.validate_length(arr2, n)\n\n    i = 0  # Pointer for arr1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for arr2\n    \n    # These will store the (n-1)-th and n-th elements of the conceptually merged list (0-indexed).\n    # The median of a 2n element list is the average of elements at indices n-1 and n.\n    element_at_n_minus_1 = 0\n    element_at_n = 0\n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the element at index 'n' and capture the one before it.\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        if i == n:  # All elements of arr1 have been considered\n            element_at_n_minus_1 = element_at_n\n            element_at_n = arr2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:  # All elements of arr2 have been considered\n            element_at_n_minus_1 = element_at_n\n            element_at_n = arr1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif arr1[i] <= arr2[j]:\n            element_at_n_minus_1 = element_at_n\n            element_at_n = arr1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else:  # arr2[j] < arr1[i]\n            element_at_n_minus_1 = element_at_n\n            element_at_n = arr2[j]\n            j += 1\n            \n    return (float(element_at_n_minus_1) + float(element_at_n)) / 2.0"}
