{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array, target) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Return the largest index i such that array[i] == target, or -1 if target not present.\n\n    Preconditions: array is a Python list sorted in ascending order; elements are comparable with target.\n    Postconditions: array is not modified. Time: O(log n). Space: O(1).\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] == target:\n            result = mid  # Found a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1 # Try to find an even larger index in the right half\n        elif array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # array[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n            \n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/794", "solution": "def text_starta_endb(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Matches a string that starts with 'a' and ends with 'b'. Returns False for empty strings.\"\"\"\n    if len(text) == 0:\n        return False\n    first = text[0]\n    last = text[-1]\n    return first == 'a' and last == 'b'"}
